ciency</strong> and <strong>flawless safety</strong>. Our premium <strong>2.5mm AC copper wires</strong> are the heart of a reliable cooling system. Designed for superior conductivity, these wires minimize power loss and prevent overheating, protecting your valuable appliance.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class=\"mt-4 space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\r\n \t<li class=\"flex items-start\"><span class=\"text-blue-500 mr-2\">⚡</span>\r\n<div><strong>Maximum Conductivity:</strong> Made from 99.9% pure electrolytic copper for peak electrical performance and lower electricity bills.</div></li>\r\n \t<li class=\"flex items-start\"><span class=\"text-blue-500 mr-2\">🛡️</span>\r\n<div><strong>Superior Safety:</strong> Features multi-layer PVC insulation that is flame-retardant, heat-resistant, and weatherproof.</div></li>\r\n \t<li class=\"flex items-start\"><span class=\"text-blue-500 mr-2\">❄️</span>\r\n<div><strong>Optimal AC Performance:</strong> The correct wire gauge prevents voltage drops, allowing your AC&#8217;s compressor and <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold\" href=\"https://atlasaircons.com/ac-blower-motor/\">blower motor</a> to function perfectly.</div></li>\r\n \t<li class=\"flex items-start\"><span class=\"text-blue-500 mr-2\">✅</span>\r\n<div><strong>ISI Certified:</strong> Guaranteed quality and adherence to the highest safety standards in <strong>India</strong>.</div></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<!-- Price Section -->\r\n<div class=\"mt-6\">\r\n<h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Indicative Price List (per meter)</h2>\r\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\r\n<table class=\"min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-300 rounded-md\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr class=\"bg-gray-100\">\r\n<th class=\"text-left py-2 px-4 font-semibold text-gray-600\">Wire Type</th>\r\n<th class=\"text-left py-2 px-4 font-semibold text-gray-600\">Ideal For</th>\r\n<th class=\"text-right py-2 px-4 font-semibold text-gray-600\">Approx. Price (INR)</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr class=\"border-t\">\r\n<td class=\"py-2 px-4 font-medium\"><strong>2.5mm 3 Core Copper Wire</strong></td>\r\n<td class=\"py-2 px-4 text-gray-600\">Up to 1.5 Ton ACs</td>\r\n<td class=\"py-2 px-4 text-right font-bold text-lg text-blue-700\">₹75 &#8211; ₹95</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"border-t bg-blue-50\">\r\n<td class=\"py-2 px-4 font-medium\"><strong>2.5mm 4 Core Copper Wire</strong></td>\r\n<td class=\"py-2 px-4 text-gray-600\">1.5 Ton to 2.5 Ton Inverter ACs</td>\r\n<td class=\"py-2 px-4 text-right font-bold text-lg text-blue-700\">₹98 &#8211; ₹120</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"text-xs text-right mt-1 text-gray-500\">*Prices are indicative and subject to change. Contact us for the latest rates.</p>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"mt-6\">\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nCall Now for Best Price: <a href=\"http://wa.me/919727257141\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">+91-97272-57141</a>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<!-- Long Description / Tabs -->\r\n<div class=\"mt-12 lg:mt-16\">\r\n<div class=\"border-b border-gray-200\"><nav class=\"-mb-px flex space-x-6\" aria-label=\"Tabs\"><button class=\"tab-button whitespace-nowrap py-4 px-1 border-b-2 font-medium text-sm border-transparent text-gray-500 hover:text-gray-700 hover:border-gray-300\">Product Details</button>\r\n<button class=\"tab-button whitespace-nowrap py-4 px-1 border-b-2 font-medium text-sm border-transparent text-gray-500 hover:text-gray-700 hover:border-gray-300\">Technical Specifications</button>\r\n<button class=\"tab-button whitespace-nowrap py-4 px-1 border-b-2 font-medium text-sm border-transparent text-gray-500 hover:text-gray-700 hover:border-gray-300\">Do&#8217;s &amp; Don&#8217;ts</button>\r\n<button class=\"tab-button whitespace-nowrap py-4 px-1 border-b-2 font-medium text-sm border-transparent text-gray-500 hover:text-gray-700 hover:border-gray-300\">Common Issues</button>\r\n<button class=\"tab-button whitespace-nowrap py-4 px-1 border-b-2 font-medium text-sm border-transparent text-gray-500 hover:text-gray-700 hover:border-gray-300\">Pros &amp; Cons</button></nav></div>\r\n<div class=\"mt-6 prose max-w-none prose-blue\">\r\n<div>\r\n<h3 class=\"font-bold text-xl\">The Unseen Hero of Your Comfort</h3>\r\nWhen you invest in an air conditioner, you&#8217;re investing in comfort. But the performance of your AC heavily relies on its components, especially the <strong>AC power cable</strong>. Using a sub-par or incorrect wire is a critical mistake that can lead to poor cooling, higher power consumption, and even create a serious fire hazard. At <strong>Atlas Aircon</strong>, we supply only the highest grade <strong>2.5mm 3 core and 4 core copper wires</strong>, ensuring your cooling system gets the clean, stable power it needs. Whether it&#8217;s a new installation in <strong>Ahmedabad</strong> or a repair in <strong>Surat</strong>, our wires provide the foundation for a long-lasting and efficient AC unit. This focus on quality components is why we are a trusted name for all <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:underline\" href=\"https://atlasaircons.com/products/ac-repair/window-air-conditioner-products.html\">window air conditioner products</a>.\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<h3 class=\"font-bold text-xl\">Technical Details</h3>\r\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\r\n<table class=\"min-w-full\">\r\n<tbody class=\"bg-white\">\r\n<tr class=\"border-t\">\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2 font-semibold\">Product Name</td>\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2\">Multi-Core Flexible Copper Wire for Air Conditioners</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"border-t bg-gray-50\">\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2 font-semibold\">Conductor Material</td>\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2\">99.9% Electrolytic Grade Copper</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"border-t\">\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2 font-semibold\">Size</td>\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2\"><strong>2.5 sq mm</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"border-t bg-gray-50\">\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2 font-semibold\">Core Options</td>\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2\"><strong>3 Core</strong> (Phase, Neutral, Earth), <strong>4 Core</strong> (Phase, Neutral, Earth, Communication/Control)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"border-t\">\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2 font-semibold\">Insulation</td>\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2\">FR (Flame Retardant) PVC Compound</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"border-t bg-gray-50\">\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2 font-semibold\">Voltage Grade</td>\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2\">Up to 1100V</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"border-t\">\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2 font-semibold\">Standards</td>\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2\">ISI Marked, Conforms to IS 694</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"border-t bg-gray-50\">\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2 font-semibold\">Application</td>\r\n<td class=\"px-4 py-2\">Residential &amp; Commercial AC Units, including Split ACs and Inverter ACs</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8\">\r\n<div>\r\n<h4 class=\"font-bold text-lg text-green-700\">Do&#8217;s ✅</h4>\r\n<ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1\">\r\n \t<li><strong>DO</strong> ensure the wire size matches your AC&#8217;s tonnage and power requirements.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>DO</strong> hire a qualified electrician for installation in cities like <strong>Vadodara</strong> or <strong>Bharuch</strong>.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>DO</strong> check for the ISI mark to guarantee quality and safety.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>DO</strong> use proper conduits and casing to protect the wire from physical damage.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<h4 class=\"font-bold text-lg text-red-700\">Don&#8217;ts ❌</h4>\r\n<ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1\">\r\n \t<li><strong>DON&#8217;T</strong> use aluminum or Copper Coated Aluminum (CCA) wires for ACs.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>DON&#8217;T</strong> use wires with joints or tapes for the main power line.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>DON&#8217;T</strong> leave the wire exposed to direct sunlight or moisture without proper casing.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>DON&#8217;T</strong> overload the wire by connecting other high-power appliances to the same circuit.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<h3 class=\"font-bold text-xl\">Common Issues from Using Wrong Wires</h3>\r\n<ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1\">\r\n \t<li><strong>Wire Overheating:</strong> Undersized wires can get dangerously hot, melting the insulation and creating a fire risk.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>Reduced Cooling Performance:</strong> Incorrect wires cause voltage drops, starving the compressor of power and leading to inefficient cooling.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>Frequent Tripping of MCB:</strong> The AC will draw more current through a poor wire, causing the circuit breaker to trip frequently.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>Permanent Damage to AC:</strong> Inconsistent power supply can permanently damage sensitive electronic components in your AC unit.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8\">\r\n<div>\r\n<h4 class=\"font-bold text-lg text-green-700\">Pros of Using Atlas Aircon Copper Wire</h4>\r\n<ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1\">\r\n \t<li><strong>Energy Savings:</strong> High conductivity means less power is wasted as heat.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>Long-Term Reliability:</strong> Protects your AC investment by providing stable power.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>Enhanced Safety:</strong> Significantly reduces the risk of electrical faults and fires.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>Peace of Mind:</strong> ISI-certified quality you can trust for your home or business in <strong>Gujarat</strong>.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<h4 class=\"font-bold text-lg text-red-700\"><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://atlasaircons.com/affordable-and-expert-ac-repair-service/\">Cons of Using Cheaper Alternatives</a></h4>\r\n<ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1\">\r\n \t<li><strong>Higher Risk of Fire:</strong> Aluminum/CCA wires overheat easily.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>Voided AC Warranty:</strong> Most manufacturers&#8217; warranties are voided by improper wiring.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>Higher Electricity Bills:</strong> Poor conductivity leads to energy wastage.</li>\r\n \t<li><strong>Costly Repairs:</strong> Can lead to expensive damage to your AC&#8217;s compressor and PCB.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<!-- FAQ Section -->\r\n<div class=\"mt-12 lg:mt-16 bg-white p-8 rounded-lg shadow-md border border-gray-200\">\r\n<h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-center mb-6\">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\r\n<div class=\"space-y-4\">\r\n<div class=\"border-b pb-4\">\r\n<h3 class=\"font-semibold text-lg\">Which wire is best for a 1.5 ton or 2 ton AC?</h3>\r\n<p class=\"text-gray-600 mt-1\">For a 1.5 ton AC, a <strong>2.5mm 3 core copper wire</strong> is generally sufficient. For a 2 ton AC or installations requiring more complex connections (like inverter ACs with communication lines), the <strong>2.5mm 4 core copper wire</strong> is the recommended choice for safety and performance.</p>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"border-b pb-4\">\r\n<h3 class=\"font-semibold text-lg\">What is the primary difference between 3 core and 4 core AC wire?</h3>\r\n<p class=\"text-gray-600 mt-1\">A <strong>3 core wire</strong> has three conductors: Phase (Live), Neutral, and Earth. A <strong>4 core wire</strong> has an additional conductor, which is often used for communication between the indoor and outdoor units in inverter ACs or for other specific control functions.</p>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"border-b pb-4\">\r\n<h3 class=\"font-semibold text-lg\">Why should I only use pure copper wire for my AC?</h3>\r\n<p class=\"text-gray-600 mt-1\">Pure <strong>copper wire</strong> offers superior electrical conductivity, lower resistance, and better heat dissipation compared to aluminum or CCA wires. This translates to higher energy efficiency, reduced risk of overheating, and a longer, safer lifespan for your air conditioner.</p>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<h3 class=\"font-semibold text-lg\">Do you provide AC copper wire near me in Surat or Ahmedabad?</h3>\r\n<p class=\"text-gray-600 mt-1\">Yes! <strong>Atlas Aircon</strong> is headquartered in <strong>Vadodara</strong> and proudly serves numerous cities including <strong>Surat, Ahmedabad, Bharuch, Ankleshwar, Vapi</strong>, and all across <strong>Gujarat</strong>. We provide fast delivery and support for all your AC component needs.</p>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<!-- Service Area Section -->\r\n<div class=\"mt-12 lg:mt-16 text-center\">\r\n<h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold\">Serving Across Gujarat and All Over India</h2>\r\n<p class=\"mt-2 text-gray-600 max-w-3xl mx-auto\">Our head office is in <strong>Vadodara</strong>, but our network is vast. We are the leading supplier of <strong>AC copper wire</strong> and other spare parts in <strong>Ahmedabad, Nadiad, Anand, Karjan, Palej, Bharuch, Ankleshwar, Dahej, Jhagadia, Rajpipla, Surat, Vapi, Valsad, Daman</strong>, and beyond.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"mt-4\"><a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline\" href=\"https://atlasaircons.com\">Contact Us Today for Bulk Inquiries &amp; Dealership!</a></div>\r\n</div>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;",
